			"type": "text",
			"text": "Barwickosteus was a placoderm discovered in the Aztec Siltstone of Antarctica, dating back to the Devonian. Its name is a reference to 'Richard Essex Barwic' a member of the original Victoria University Antarctic Expeditions and the Greek word for Bone. Its head armor is estimated to have been 4 centimeters long, though a few specimens that are about 6 centimeters could also be attributed to this species."
